// Golden eval set — spec section 5. Written by reading the indexed corpus
// (astral-sh/uv issue threads), not by imagining questions.
//
// 32 questions: 26 answerable, 6 unanswerable, 7 tagged thread_reply.
//
// The unanswerable ones are onboarding questions a new hire would plausibly ask
// a team-memory tool — on-call, expenses, leave — which a Python packaging
// issue tracker genuinely cannot answer. They are deliberately not "uv
// questions about uncovered features", because the corpus is broad enough that
// such a question often half-matches and tests nothing crisp.
//
// thread_reply marks questions whose answer is in a reply rather than the
// opening post. Those are the ones that prove chunking keeps a question with
// its answer.

{"q": "Can uv be used as a task runner like npm scripts?", "expect_sources": ["github:astral-sh/uv:5903", "github:astral-sh/uv:10211"], "answerable": true}
{"q": "Why does uv need its own build backend instead of using an existing one?", "expect_sources": ["github:astral-sh/uv:3957"], "answerable": true}
